//! Runtime support for bindings generated by `blazon`.
//!
//! Everything here is JVM- or JDK-specific and knows nothing about Bazel or
//! Starlark: creating a JVM from a `libjvm` chosen at runtime, typed handles
//! and subtyping, global references, turning pending Java exceptions into
//! [`Error`]s, cached class and member IDs, the reflection path for members
//! that are not public, and typed handles for the standard Java types
//! ([`java`]).
//!
//! The process's JVM is registered once (`Jvm::start` does it). Statics and
//! constructors take the `JNIEnv` they make references in; everything else
//! attaches its thread through [`vm::env`]. A handle owns one local reference
//! and releases it when dropped, so it is valid only on the thread that made
//! it; store a [`Global`] to keep an object longer, and open a [`vm::scope`]
//! around work that holds many references at once.

pub mod conv;
mod error;
mod handle;
pub mod implement;
pub mod java;
mod jvm;
pub mod member;
